<a:ObjectID>CC7ED728-3531-4178-B671-2EF34EABE25E</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>LIFECYCLE_PHASE</a:Name>
<a:Code>LIFECYCLE_PHASE</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1762783496</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1762783498</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A type of part of the whole life GHG emission footprint of a product, used to account for all the direct and indirect GHG emissions involved with the creation, distribution, use and disposal of a product.

For example: 
WtT (well to tank) covers the GHG emissions footprint arising from the manufacture and distribution of a product. This includes the emissions from the production and transformation of natural resources into raw materials of the product manufacturing process.
TtW (tank to wheel) covers the use or consumption of the product. </a:Comment>
<a:History>ORG {79BFC7FC-98FA-4085-AB82-436DF44ABE39}
DAT 1762783498</a:History>
<a:TotalSavingCurrency/>
