<o:Table Id="o104">
<a:ObjectID>C5F546B4-AA51-4A77-84FF-4A6675041D34</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>APPLICATION_METHOD</a:Name>
<a:Code>APPLICATION_METHOD</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1762783496</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Elton.Manoku</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1762783498</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Elton.Manoku</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A method for calculation of GHG emissions resulting from the use of a fuel. A method may be either an input method or an output method. Input methods use a given quantity of fuel consumed. Output methods calculate the quantity of fuel consumed to achieve a designated output from a given equipment consumption rate. An example of an output method is vehicle distance where the fuel consumed is calculated from a given distance and vehicle mileage rate.

Sets of consumption rates are defined for application equipment types and fuel products that can be applied to one or more regions.</a:Comment>
<a:History>ORG {66A2BE2C-9F06-4CD9-93A1-BEC8F174890E}
DAT 1762783498</a:History>
<a:TotalSavingCurrency/>
